hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"235","We are Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, we are Waki’, we are Hisham bin Urwa. H. Ali bin Khashram told us, Waki’ told us. H. Salam bin Junada, Abu Muawiyah, told us. H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab, daughter of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the woman she sees in a dream. What does the man see? He said: “If she sees water, let her bathe.” She said: I said: Women are exposed, and do women have a wet dream? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May your right hand rest in peace, and its child will be like it, then.” This is a comprehensive hadith, except that Al-Dawrqi did not say: Then, and the end of Malik’s hadith, when he said: If she saw water, and he did not mention what After that, from the hadith"
